# Calls to the gateway (port 3000), the only public entry point.
# Paste a fresh Auth0 access token (the long eyJ… string). Don't commit a real one.
# /me needs a token from a logged-in person: log in through the app and copy it,
# or use `auth0 test token`. Tokens from the API's Test tab are machine tokens → 403 on /me.
@token = PASTE-ACCESS-TOKEN

### Public endpoint, no token needed
GET http://localhost:3000/health

### Catalog (public): categories
GET http://localhost:3000/catalog/categories

### Catalog: all services, or one category's
GET http://localhost:3000/catalog/services?category=canalizacao

### Catalog: one service page
GET http://localhost:3000/catalog/services/desentupimento-lavatorio-sanita

### Catalog: municipalities (pilot = bookings open there)
GET http://localhost:3000/catalog/municipalities

### Catalog: is this postal code served? (Coimbra is the pilot)
GET http://localhost:3000/catalog/areas/3000-123

### Catalog: home search, text and postal code are both optional
GET http://localhost:3000/catalog/search?q=canalizacao&postalCode=3000-123

### No token → 401
GET http://localhost:3000/whoami

### Any valid token → 200 with its claims
GET http://localhost:3000/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Tampered token → 401
GET http://localhost:3000/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}x

### My profile → 404 until I register, then 200 (403 with a machine token)
GET http://localhost:3000/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Register my profile → 201 (auth0Id comes from the token, not the body)
POST http://localhost:3000/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "joao@example.com", "name": "João" }

### Register again → 409 from users-service, passed through by the gateway
POST http://localhost:3000/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "joao@example.com" }

### Change my name / phone → 200 (email can't be changed here: it belongs to Auth0)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "João Pedro", "phone": "+351912345678" }

### Apply as a professional → 201, status "applied" (needs a profile first; NIF must be valid)
POST http://localhost:3000/me/professional
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "nif": "123456789", "activityRegistered": true, "businessName": "Canalizações Exemplo", "insuranceValidUntil": "2027-12-31" }

### My professional profile → 200, or 404 if I never applied
GET http://localhost:3000/me/professional
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Edit my professional profile
PATCH http://localhost:3000/me/professional
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bio": "Canalizador há 10 anos em Coimbra." }

### Documents, step 1: ask for an upload link (sizeBytes must be the file's exact size)
POST http://localhost:3000/me/professional/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "id_card", "contentType": "application/pdf", "sizeBytes": 12345, "fileName": "cc.pdf" }

### Documents, step 2: PUT the file to upload.url from the answer, with header Content-Type: application/pdf
### e.g.  curl -X PUT -H "Content-Type: application/pdf" --data-binary "@cc.pdf" "<upload.url>"

### Documents, step 3: confirm (paste document.id) → status "pending"
POST http://localhost:3000/me/professional/documents/PASTE-DOCUMENT-ID/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### My documents
GET http://localhost:3000/me/professional/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Link to view one of my documents (valid for 5 minutes)
GET http://localhost:3000/me/professional/documents/PASTE-DOCUMENT-ID/download-url
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Am I an admin? → 200 with my permissions, 403 without the admin role (see README "Admins")
GET http://localhost:3000/admin/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Booking, summary step: what would I be booking? (saves nothing)
POST http://localhost:3000/bookings/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceSlug": "desentupimento-lavatorio-sanita",
  "address": { "street": "Rua da Sofia 10", "details": "2.º Esq.", "postalCode": "3000-389" },
  "scheduledStart": "2026-12-01T15:00:00Z",
  "notes": "Tocar à campainha"
}

### Booking: book it, 201 with status "pending_payment" (use a date at least 2 hours from now)
POST http://localhost:3000/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceSlug": "desentupimento-lavatorio-sanita",
  "address": { "street": "Rua da Sofia 10", "details": "2.º Esq.", "postalCode": "3000-389" },
  "scheduledStart": "2026-12-01T15:00:00Z"
}

### My bookings
GET http://localhost:3000/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One booking, with its status history
GET http://localhost:3000/bookings/PASTE-BOOKING-ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Job offers waiting for my answer (as a professional)
GET http://localhost:3000/me/professional/offers?status=pending
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Take a job (the answer includes the full address)
POST http://localhost:3000/me/professional/offers/PASTE-OFFER-ID/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Pass on a job (the next professional is asked)
POST http://localhost:3000/me/professional/offers/PASTE-OFFER-ID/decline
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Work settings: where, what and when I work
GET http://localhost:3000/me/professional/work-settings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Where I work (replaces the list; codes from GET /catalog/municipalities)
PUT http://localhost:3000/me/professional/areas
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "municipalityCodes": ["0603"] }

### What I do (replaces the list; ids from GET /catalog/services)
PUT http://localhost:3000/me/professional/services
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "serviceTypeIds": ["PASTE-SERVICE-ID"] }

### My weekly timetable (replaces the week; weekday 1 = Monday ... 7 = Sunday)
PUT http://localhost:3000/me/professional/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slots": [
  { "weekday": 1, "start": "09:00", "end": "13:00" },
  { "weekday": 1, "start": "14:00", "end": "18:00" },
  { "weekday": 6, "start": "10:00", "end": "13:00" }
] }

### Time off
POST http://localhost:3000/me/professional/time-off
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startsAt": "2027-08-01T00:00:00Z", "endsAt": "2027-08-15T00:00:00Z", "reason": "Férias" }

### Admin: applications waiting for review (oldest first)
GET http://localhost:3000/admin/professionals?status=applied
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Admin: one application, with documents and what is still missing
GET http://localhost:3000/admin/professionals/PASTE-PROFESSIONAL-ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Admin: accept (or reject, with a reason) one document
POST http://localhost:3000/admin/professionals/PASTE-PROFESSIONAL-ID/documents/PASTE-DOCUMENT-ID/review
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "decision": "accepted" }

### Admin: approve → 200, or 409 while a required document has no accepted file
POST http://localhost:3000/admin/professionals/PASTE-PROFESSIONAL-ID/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Admin: reject, with a reason the applicant will see
POST http://localhost:3000/admin/professionals/PASTE-PROFESSIONAL-ID/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "O comprovativo de atividade está ilegível. Envia uma nova fotografia." }

### Stop users-service, then → 503
GET http://localhost:3000/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
